{"parentUuid": "6b5595de-c962-4541-bde8-d1053bd4801b", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_01HnQeEY9002X8j1rH7pvWvE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`beat_tools/bpm.py` estimates tempo from the onset envelope and folds into 70–180 (so a 70-bpm half-time reading of a 140 trap loop is fine either way, and 248 → 124). It returns `None` for files under 2 s. On the 5 test files it gets the 4 labeled ones exactly and calls the untagged lofi chop 84. The renamer only runs it with `--detect-bpm`, since loading ~300 loops with librosa takes a couple of minutes."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2544, "cache_read_input_tokens": 32520, "output_tokens": 111, "service_tier": "standard"}}, "requestId": "req_011CrwvazEpEyBDsIDngkrOL", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "8da13f3a-e125-4e64-bb26-50173e92fe58", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T02:42:32.546Z", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/divadbaroon/Projects/beat-tools", "sessionId": "2b9fa083-4e24-4b79-b25b-928a8c238f36", "version": "2.1.278", "gitBranch": "main"}
